cl inlines the closure's call operator away and emits no symbol for it, so there is nothing on its side to compare - the diff is one line, cxx1's name with no answering line from cl, which is the same reason lambda.nocl and the other closure cases record. The two functions this case exists to check, viaTemplate and viaLambda, agree with cl; what cl and cxx1 would call the closure if both emitted one is recorded in default-arg-declares.nonames, measured against clang for this ABI
